segments.text:
V. 21.
As thou art in me—This alſo is to be underſtood, in a Way of Similitude, and not of Sameneſs or Equality. That the world may believe—Here Chriſt prays for the World. Obſerve the Sum of his whole Prayer,
1. Receive me into thy own and my Glory;
2. Let my Apoſtles ſhare therein;
3. And all other Believers;
4. And let all the World believe.
